## Fix #1.5: Update UCR Prompts with Format Standard (NEW)

### File: `/opt/data/b-local/b-local-docs/docs/UCX/review/UCR_PROMPT_BRD_PROJECT.md`

**Add section after "Output Requirements"** (~line 79):

```markdown
### Finding ID Format (REQUIRED)

All personas MUST use this ID format: `{PREFIX}-P{PRIORITY}-{NNN}`

| Component | Rule | Example |
|-----------|------|---------|
| PREFIX | Persona abbreviation (2-4 chars) | ARCH, AUD, TL, OP |
| PRIORITY | P0, P1, or P2 | P0 |
| NNN | 3-digit sequence (001-999) | 001 |

**Examples**:
- Architect: `ARCH-P0-001`, `ARCH-P1-002`
- Auditor: `AUD-P0-001`, `AUD-P0-002`
- Operator: `OP-P0-001`, `OP-P1-001`

**INCORRECT formats** (do NOT use):
- `P0-OP-001` ❌ (priority first)
- `**[P0-1]**` ❌ (bracket format)
- `P0-1` ❌ (missing prefix)
```

**Update each persona output format section** to include explicit ID format example.

### Persona-Specific Updates

| Persona | Current Table Header | Updated Header |
|---------|---------------------|----------------|
| Architect | `\| ID \| Finding \|` | `\| ID (ARCH-P0-NNN) \| Finding \|` |
| Auditor | `\| ID \| Regulation \|` | `\| ID (AUD-P0-NNN) \| Regulation \|` |
| Operator | `\| ID \| Finding \|` | `\| ID (OP-P0-NNN) \| Finding \|` |
| All others | Similar pattern | Add prefix hint |

